# scripts/

Repo helpers that are **not** part of the shipped package. Nothing in
`src/PACKAGE_NAME_PLACEHOLDER/` may import from here.

Two kinds live here, and the distinction decides how you write the file:

| Kind | How it runs | Dependencies |
|---|---|---|
| Needs the project | `uv run python scripts/foo.py` | the project env (`uv.lock`) |
| Standalone | `uv run scripts/foo.py` | its own PEP 723 header |

A standalone helper declares its dependencies inline, so it works in a fresh
clone before `uv sync` has ever run:

```python
#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=PYTHON_FLOOR_PLACEHOLDER"
# dependencies = ["httpx>=0.28"]
# ///
```

A PEP 723 script must not `import PACKAGE_NAME_PLACEHOLDER` unless the package
is listed in its own `dependencies` - it runs in an isolated environment that
does not contain your project.

Anything worth running twice gets a `just` recipe so it shows up in
`just --list`.
